<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Login | <%= appInfo.name %></title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: linear-gradient(135deg, #f0e6dd 0%, #e0eef7 100%);
            --panel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
            --border: #d2c3b8;
            --accent: #0c7489;
            --accent-soft: #d9eff3;
            --text: #24313a;
            --muted: #62707a;
            --danger: #8a2b12;
        }

        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: grid;
            place-items: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .shell {
            width: min(980px, 100%);
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
            gap: 18px;
        }
        .panel {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 28px;
            padding: 28px;
            box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        }
        .pill {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 34px;
            padding: 0 12px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            background: var(--accent-soft);
            color: var(--accent);
            font-size: 0.84rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        }
        h1 {
            margin: 12px 0 8px;
        }
        p, li, label {
            color: var(--muted);
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        form {
            display: grid;
            gap: 14px;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        label {
            display: grid;
            gap: 6px;
            font-weight: 700;
        }
        input {
            width: 100%;
            min-height: 48px;
            padding: 0 14px;
            border-radius: 16px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            background: white;
            font: inherit;
            color: var(--text);
        }
        button, .link-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            min-height: 46px;
            padding: 0 16px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            border: 1px solid var(--accent);
            background: var(--accent);
            color: white;
            font: inherit;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        .secondary {
            background: transparent;
            color: var(--text);
            border-color: var(--border);
        }
        .actions {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        .error {
            padding: 14px 16px;
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: #fff0ec;
            border: 1px solid #e7b6a8;
            color: var(--danger);
        }
        .mono {
            font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
            font-size: 0.94rem;
            word-break: break-word;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="shell">
        <section class="panel">
            <span class="pill">Custom Sign-in Form</span>
            <h1>Use your own login page</h1>
            <p>This page is rendered by your app, not Cognito Hosted UI. When you submit the form, the server calls the Cognito User Pool API directly with the configured auth flow.</p>

            <% if (error) { %>
                <div class="error">
                    <strong>Login failed</strong>
                    <div class="mono"><%= error %></div>
                </div>
            <% } %>

            <form method="post" action="/login">
                <label>
                    Username
                    <input type="text" name="username" value="<%= formValues.username %>" autocomplete="username" required>
                </label>
                <label>
                    Password
                    <input type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required>
                </label>
                <button type="submit">Sign in with Cognito</button>
            </form>

            <div class="actions">
                <a class="link-btn secondary" href="/">Back to Home</a>
                <a class="link-btn secondary" href="/public-page">Open Public Page</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel">
            <h2>Configuration used by this form</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Base URL:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.baseUrl %></span></li>
                <li><strong>Region:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.region %></span></li>
                <li><strong>User Pool ID:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.userPoolId %></span></li>
                <li><strong>App Client ID:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.clientId %></span></li>
                <li><strong>Auth flow:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.authFlow %></span></li>
            </ul>
            <p>For this demo to work, the Cognito App Client must allow direct username/password authentication. If Cognito returns MFA or password-reset challenges, the app will show a clear error because those flows are not implemented here.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
